{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Mechanism and measurements (investigation before claim).\n\nDecision rule: `pass3_decide` in src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py returns `dropped / veto:cited-reference-inaccurate` whenever the Pass-2 binary `cited_reference_accurate == \"no\"`. It compares no locations. The verifier prompts decide what that answer means, and neither says whose citation is in question: the agentic prompt says \"for a finding that cites a specific code reference, VERIFY the citation\"; the single-turn prompt says \"answer it only when the finding cites a specific code reference\".\n\nSidecar evidence: the 5 dropped findings on this ticket (28d0-148d f49e9d9ad9502c56e; c159-1621 fcf9e907f6cdeeee1, feb2e8e8f9645fdf2; 2a3d-9d00 fc278276e288565ef, f760ac2553d5604cd) all carry cited_reference_accurate=no together with evidence_entails_finding=yes and validity 0.67-1.0. Store-wide across 9,757 saved REVIEW_RESULT sidecars the veto fired 1,489 times; 448 of those had evidence_entails_finding=yes and 519 had validity >= 0.5.\n\nReproduction: scratch probe running the real Pass-2 prompt through the kernel verify_findings + pass3_decide, configured standard model (bedrock sonnet-4-6), agentic runs inside a local gate_read_root session. Fixture: plan with case 1 (nonexistent tests/unit/test_init_ensures_seam.py), case 2 (CHANGELOG.md:371) and case 4 (AGENTS.md:215) mis-citations, 3 correct findings reporting them, plus a control whose OWN evidence cites src/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py:40-41 for AUTHOR_GUIDES (wrong).\n\nUnfixed prompts, 3 samples each:\n- agentic: runs where all 3 correct findings survived = 0/3 (7 of 9 correct-finding verdicts were cra=no -> vetoed); control vetoed 3/3.\n- single-turn: all 3 survived in 1/3 runs (4 of 9 vetoed).\n\nScoped prompts (rule: the question tests the finding's own evidence; a wrong plan citation the finding reports is yes, never no), 3 samples each:\n- agentic: all 3 survived 3/3 runs (9/9 cra=yes); control vetoed 3/3 (cra=no).\n- single-turn: all 3 survived 3/3 (cra=insufficient or na, none vetoed); control cra=no in 2/3, dropped in 3/3.\n\nPrior intent: epic messy-moose-jig and evals/plan-review-gate/harnesses/three_pass.py aim Pass-2 skepticism at the FINDING and scope the veto to a code citation present in the finding's evidence. Nothing documents vetoing a finding because the plan's citation is wrong. Code fix scope: the two prompts + the docs sentence, no change to pass3_decide."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793503939320680001,"uuid":"0f283fe5-8f9e-4a80-8aff-a339cc7dd985"}